Package: gofdegrad
Title: Goodness-of-Fit Tests for Degradation Models by Similarity and Bootstrap
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Amedée Rytrace", "Tito", , "tito.amedee-rytrace@univ-pau.fr", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Goodness-of-fit test for degradation models of Zheng, Wang,
    Chen and Xie (2026, Quality and Reliability Engineering International):
    the observed trajectories are compared with trajectories simulated under
    the fitted candidate model through Kolmogorov-Smirnov and Cramer-von Mises
    type similarity measures, and the critical values are obtained by
    parametric bootstrap. Seven candidate models are available (Wiener, gamma,
    inverse Gaussian, variance-gamma and Meixner processes, and Wiener and
    gamma processes with power-law time transformation), with possibly
    irregular inspection times common to all trajectories; any other model can
    be tested by giving its own estimation and simulation functions. The
    simulations rely on the package 'levysim' and the maximum likelihood
    estimators on the package 'levyfit'. Level and power studies by Monte
    Carlo simulation are also provided.
